0 37 208 [
[(Here we apply an amplitude envelope to protect against)]
[(discontinuities at the loop point. The envelope is just a)]
[(cosine wave from -90 degrees to +90 degrees, \050-pi/2 to pi/2)]
[(radians\051, i.e., the part that is zero or positive in sign.)]
[(The [cos~] object's input is in cycles \050units of 2pi radians\051)]
[(so -1/4 to +1/4 addresses the desired part of the waveform.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
